PRE-TABLE CHECK -- ppcrldimimask
Written BEFORE table 1 runs, so this file's own mtime proves the order.

THE DIFF UNDER TEST is the FOUR COORDINATED EDITS in X(rldimi) in src/cpus/cpu_ppc_instr.c:
  1. `int m, n = sh;`                       /*  1: keep SH  */
  2. `while (n-- != 0)`                     /*  2: consume the copy  */
  3. `m = (m + 1) & 63;`                    /*  3: circular increment  */
  4. `while (m != ((64 - sh) & 63));`       /*  4: successor modulo 64  */

A partial repair changing only some of these does not work: saving SH without the circular
increment hits `(uint64_t)1 << -1` at MB=40, SH=40 (undefined behaviour in C).

--------------------------------------------------------------------- SIBLING PARITY

The sibling operations in opcode 30:
  rldicl   repaired in #522 (e777ff0) by building mask in tmp2
  rldicr   correct in tree: clears bits outside MASK(0, ME)
  rldimi   this round: bitfield insert under MASK(MB, 63-SH) with wrapping
  rlwimi   sibling 32-bit insert: separate defect (rotates 64 bits wide and omits
           high-word insertion on wrapping masks), scheduled as separate round `ppcrlwimiwidth`.

--------------------------------------------------------------------- CLAIM -> ROW

1. "X(rldimi)'s rotate loop post-decrements sh to -1 on exit for every SH"
   -> ROWED by every row where SH != 0.
2. "Non-wrapping encodings (MB <= 63-SH) overwrite low SH destination bits"
   -> ROWED as `nowrap sh8 mb0`, `nowrap sh32 mb0`, `nowrap sh16 mb16`, `pres nowrap`.
3. "Wrapping encodings (MB > 63-SH) omit insertion into positions 0..63-SH"
   -> ROWED as `wrap sh40 mb40` (worked case 40,40), `wrap sh63 mb63`, `wrap full`,
      `wrap sh48 mb32`, `pres wrap`.
4. "rldimi with MB=0, SH=0 agrees on broken build by coincidence"
   -> ROWED as `nowrap sh0 mb0` (green on committed, green on fix).
5. "One-character mutant 64 -> 63 drops architectural bit 63"
   -> ROWED as `M_MUT63` leg in kill table, tested against `nowrap single` and `nowrap sh0 mb0`.
6. "Full census across sweeps and diagonals"
   -> ROWED as `census run`, `census wrong`, `census zero` (495 cells driven).

--------------------------------------------------------- GUARD FIELD vs BODY FIELD

This instruction is a pure computational transformation in user/supervisor mode:
  Inputs:  cpu->cd.ppc.gpr[rs], cpu->cd.ppc.gpr[ra], sh, mb, rc
  Outputs: cpu->cd.ppc.gpr[ra], and CR0 when rc=1

The census walks the cross-product space (MB sweeps, SH sweeps, diagonal, anti-diagonal).

